@title  PCSE00235 - title -> FIGHT -> VERSUS -> Solo Match -> a fight played to the result screen
@game   PCSE00235
@shot-every 120

# WHAT THIS RECIPE IS FOR
# ----------------------
# The GAMEPLAY recipe for Dead or Alive 5 Plus: it walks the front end with the defaults, lets
# the fight start, throws a punch/kick flurry, lets the match play out, and ASSERTS the result save.
#
# WHAT A RUN OF THIS LOOKS LIKE (2026-09-24, desktop headless):
#   f000150          the Tecmo Koei logo
#   f000600-f001500  the Team Ninja intro movie `ninja_vi.mp4`, then the Team Ninja logo
#   ~f001663         the autosave notice (a MsgDialog, answered OK)
#   f001800          title screen, "PRESS START"            <- start
#   f001860          play style prompt, casual is default   <- cross, then cross on the OK
#   f002100          main menu, cursor on STORY             <- down to FIGHT, cross
#   f002280-f003000  VERSUS, Solo Match, character select (Kasumi vs Ryane), stage select
#   f003120          stage select                           <- cross
#   f003300          Ayane's intro close-up
#   f003600          LIVE FIGHT (desktop; the browser starts it later - see the asserts)
#   f003700-f003932  the flurry: triangle / circle alternately, every 12 frames
#   ~f006300         Kasumi K.O.'d - the CPU wins the match
#   ~f006600-f007050 "You got a new title! KASUMI NEWBIE", save_sys.dat written (desktop f6733)
#   f007800          asserted: a SaveWrite at or after f6000 (the match result)
#
# RENDERING (2026-09-24, desktop headless, recompiled path): the stage, tigers, both fighters
# (lit, in costume) and the HUD all draw. What it took, for the record: a depth clear from the
# surface's background depth, U8_A targets storing alpha, strided and sub-rectangle textures,
# UNTYPED vertex attributes, stacked cube-map targets, local memory, 4-lane swizzles, F16
# sources on scalar ops, texcoords the vertex does not write, the colour-mask bit order (A is
# bit 0 - the hair was cyan without it) and SetFormat's extension bit on copied textures.

# Both fighters' health: u16 pairs, current then max (270 = full), 0xd8 apart, found by a
# two-run memory diff (no input vs the flurry below, same frame; a mirror of P1's sits at
# 0x81b0ce60). In that diff it was P1 - KASUMI, us - who lost health: pressing buttons changes
# what the CPU does, and it landed hits on us. The addresses hold in a run that RENDERS every
# frame (the desktop app, the browser): this title reads its render targets back, and a runner
# that never renders (`play`, a session with no shots) takes a different path and reads 0 here.
# Buttons (DOA5+ Vita): triangle PUNCH, circle KICK, square HOLD, cross THROW.
# >>> DESKTOP-RUNNER OBSERVATIONS, NOT ASSERTED: the browser lays the fight data out elsewhere
# (its render cadence differs, and this title reads its render targets back), so these read
# leftovers there. They are kept because on the desktop they show the exchange frame by frame.
@watch p1hp    u16 0x81b1d37c
@watch p1hpmax u16 0x81b1d37e
@watch p2hp    u16 0x81b1d454
@watch p2hpmax u16 0x81b1d456

